# Integer128 remainder sign

Takes a 30-digit value and its negation modulo 7 to verify the remainder
keeps the dividend sign in both cases, producing 5 and -5.

>>> source
dividend: int128 = 100000000000000000000000000000
neg_dividend: int128 = -100000000000000000000000000000
divisor: int128 = 7

// Verifies the remainder of two positive operands.
pos_remainder: int128 = dividend % divisor
print(pos_remainder)

// Verifies the remainder takes the dividend sign for a negative dividend.
neg_remainder: int128 = neg_dividend % divisor
print(neg_remainder)

<<< stdout
5
-5

<<< stderr
